{"key":"DebugLogWindow","text":"## DebugLogWindow\n\nThe **Debug Log Window** captures Unity's `Debug.Log`, warnings, and errors\nin real-time with colour coding and text-selection support.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.04 | Clear removes all entries, Copy copies the full log as plain text, ⇄ Wrap toggles word wrap. Title turns green when new logs arrive while the window is in the background.\nLog Output | 0.50, 0.55 | Real-time Unity log capture. White = Debug.Log, Red = errors and exceptions. Auto-scrolls to the newest entry. Select text with the mouse; drag near the edge to auto-scroll while selecting long entries.\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **Clear** — remove all captured log entries\n- **Copy** — copy the full log to the clipboard as plain text\n- **⇄ Wrap** — toggle word wrap (wrapped = vertical scroll only; unwrapped = horizontal + vertical)\n\n---\n\n### Log Colours\n\n- **White** — standard `Debug.Log` messages\n- **Red** — `Debug.LogError` and unhandled exceptions\n\n---\n\n### Features\n\n- Subscribes to `Application.logMessageReceived` — captures logs from all sources\n- Auto-scrolls to the bottom as new messages arrive\n- While drag-selecting text near the viewport edges, the scroll view accelerates to let you select long entries\n- When the window is in the background (not focused), the title indicator turns **green** when new logs arrive; resets when you bring the window to front\n\n---","screenshot":""}